@startuml 00-system-overview
' Component / deployment view of the whole system.
' Render: plantuml docs/diagrams/00-system-overview.puml
'    or:  paste into https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml

title Shopping List — system overview

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Sans
skinparam ArrowColor #2f5fd8
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #2f5fd8
  BackgroundColor #eef2fd
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #0f9d76
  BackgroundColor #e4f6f0
}

actor "Shopper" as user

node "Browser" {
  [React 19 + Redux Toolkit\n<size:11>Vite bundle served by nginx</size>] as client
}

node "Docker Compose network" {

  package "Screen 1 — catalog" {
    [catalog-api\n<size:11>.NET 10 Web API</size>\n<size:11>EF Core 10</size>] as catalog
    database "SQL Server 2022\n<size:11>CatalogDb</size>" as sql
  }

  package "Screen 2 — orders" {
    [orders-api\n<size:11>NestJS 11</size>\n<size:11>ports & adapters</size>] as orders
    database "Elasticsearch 8\n<size:11>index: orders</size>\n<size:11><b>default driver</b></size>" as es
    database "MongoDB 7\n<size:11>orders.orders</size>\n<size:11>alternative driver</size>" as mongo
  }
}

user --> client : uses

client --> catalog : GET /api/categories\nGET /api/products
client --> orders  : POST /api/orders\nGET /api/orders/{id}

catalog --> sql : EF Core\n(SqlClient, pooled)

orders ..> es    : NOSQL_DRIVER=elasticsearch
orders ..> mongo : NOSQL_DRIVER=mongodb

note right of orders
  Exactly **one** adapter is bound to the
  ORDER_REPOSITORY token at composition
  time. The service layer above it cannot
  tell which store is live.
end note

note bottom of catalog
  The two backends share **nothing** —
  no database, no library, no deployment
  unit. They meet only in the browser.
end note

@enduml
